FixDock is an unofficial fork for personal use. It is not endorsed by
the Vorssaint maintainers and is not an official release. The Vorssaint
name, logo, icon, bundle identity, and signing identity are not used
for this app. See TRADEMARKS.md in this repository, which is the
upstream trademark notice and is unchanged.

Modifications in this tree, relative to that upstream commit:

- Rebranded the app to FixDock.
- Bundle identifier is io.github.qaws81877.fixdock
  (developer builds use io.github.qaws81877.fixdock.dev).
- Removed the upstream name from the running app, the app icon, the
  signing identity, the update feed, and network endpoints.
- Reduced the app to the menu-bar shell: status item, settings,
  feature catalog and install system, onboarding, permission guide,
  shared UI, one global shortcut, and the build and uninstall scripts.
- Removed every feature module from the tree, including audio and the
  mixer, the system monitor, fan control, the notch, window, Dock, and
  switcher tools, mouse and scroll tools, Homebrew, app updates, the
  uninstaller, ports, wallpaper, and agent usage.
- URL cleaner is included, adapted from upstream. It rewrites copied
  links on this Mac and does not send them anywhere.
- The other planned tools are listed in the catalog and can be marked
  installed, but their modules are not in this build and do not run.
  Order after URL cleaner: quit/close protection, cleaning mode, text
  snippets, AirDrop auto-zip (new; not in upstream), cleaner, screenshot,
  screen recorder.
- Menu-bar positioning is the system popover. The upstream drift
  correction and extra status items were not carried over.
- Kept English and Korean only.
- Replaced the icon with FixDock's own artwork (Resources/AppIcon.png).
  No upstream brand images, showcase video, or highlight graphics are
  included.
- Signing in build.sh is ad-hoc unless FIXDOCK_CODESIGN_IDENTITY is set
  to an identity you control. The upstream signing setup is not included.
- No telemetry, analytics, or crash reporting. The one network use is
  FixDock's own update check, described in PRIVACY.md.
- 2026-10-31: Added FixDock's own update check, download and install,
  against FixDock's own GitHub releases. The upstream update feed is
  still not used.

Third-party bundled assets and fonts:

vorssaint-utils did not bundle a third-party font. Its brand images and
demo media are upstream trademarks and are not in FixDock. The menu bar
uses FixDock's own mark (Resources/Icons/fixdock-mark.svg).

FixDock bundles a few icons from Reicon (github.com/dqev/reicon), MIT
License, Copyright (c) 2025 REICON. They are in Resources/Icons with the
license text in Resources/Icons/LICENSE-reicon.txt. No other third-party
asset is bundled.
The app icon (Resources/AppIcon.png) and the menu bar mark
(Resources/Icons/fixdock-mark.svg) were drawn for FixDock, are covered by
FixDock's GPL-3.0-or-later license, and contain no upstream artwork.

